          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em torsor
            (in the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+sets"} category of sets
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            that has forgotten its identity element; given any (non-empty) torsor with respect to a group
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            by making what is known as a
            %em trivialisation
            of the torsor, which roughly corresponds to choosing an identity element. That we wish to keep track of the choice is precisely the reason for working with torsors.
          %p
            Something analogous is present in the theory of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+fibration"} fibrations
          %p
            The notion of a torsor can be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalisation"} internalised
            to any category with products, and more generally to any category in which the notion of an internal group can be made good sense of. We discuss this general notion below, after first discussing the notion in the category of sets.
          %h2#in_the_category_of_sets In the category of sets
          %h3#twosorted_definition Two-sorted definition
          %p
            Given a group
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "-torsor" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+action"} free
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transitive+action"} transitive action
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            on an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+set"} inhabited set
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+theory"} algebraic theory
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
              %em
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                \-torsor
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+set"} inhabited set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              together with an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo :
                    %mi G
                    %mo ×
                    %mi T
                    %mo →
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a: G \times T \rightarrow T
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              such that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shear+map"} shear map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mn 2
                    %mo :
                    %mi G
                    %mo ×
                    %mi T
                    %mo →
                    %mi T
                    %mo ×
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \times p_2: G \times T \rightarrow T \times T
              is an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_2
              is the canonical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projection"} projection
              map
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                      %mo ×
                      %mi T
                      %mo →
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \times T \rightarrow T
          %p
            Since we can state that the shear map is an isomorphism by positing an inverse map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi T
                  %mo ×
                  %mi T
                  %mo →
                  %mi T
                  %mo ×
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: T \times T \to T \times G
            and giving equations that state it is an inverse, the only non-equational part of the definition is that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            be inhabited. If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            is not required to be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited"} inhabited
            (that is, possibly
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+set"} empty
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudo-torsor"} pseudo-torsor
          %p
            Asking that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shear+map"} shear map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ×
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \times p_2
            be an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            is the same as to say that the action is both
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+action"} free
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transitive+action"} transitive
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+action"} regular
            if
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+set"} inhabited
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injectivity"} injectivity
            of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shear+map"} shear map
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surjectivity"} surjectivity
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shear+map"} shear map
          %p
          #RemarkTorsorIsomorphicToStructureGroup.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              is non-empty, we shall prove
              %a{:href => "#TrivialisationInSets"} below
              that it follows from the definition that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              is isomorphic to the underlying set of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              %em trivialisation
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              %a{:href => "#TrivialisationInSets"} below
              for more details.
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              As a consequence of Remark
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RemarkTorsorIsomorphicToStructureGroup"}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heap"} heap
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              An
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+space"} affine space
              of dimension
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              over a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              is a torsor for the additive group
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi k
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k^n
              = succeed "." do
                %em translation
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+measurement"} unit of measurement
              is (typically) an element in an
              = succeed "-torsor," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mo ×
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^\times
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo ×
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^\times
              the multiplicative group of non-zero
              = succeed "s:" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+number"} real number
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
              any unit and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r \in \mathbb{R}
              any non-vanishing real number, also
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mi u
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r u
              is a unit. And for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi u
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u_1
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi u
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u_2
              two units, one is expressed in terms of the other by a unique
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo ≠
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r \neq 0
              as
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi u
                        %mn 1
                      %mo =
                      %mi r
                      %msub
                        %mi u
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u_1 = r u_2
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass"} mass
              we have the unit of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kilogram"} kilogram
              and that of gram and there is a unique number,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1000
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r = 1000
              with
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi kg
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1000
                    %mi g
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    kg = 1000 g.
            %p
          %p
          #ExampleTorsorFromAGroup.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              on itself equips the underlying set of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              with the structure of a
              = succeed "-torsor." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              We shall see in Remark
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RemarkGroupStructureFromTrivialisation"}
              that all torsors actually arise as in Example
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ExampleTorsorFromAGroup"}
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              Given two isomorphic objects
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              in any category
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              form a torsor (both for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Aut(X)
              and for
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Aut
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Aut(Y)
              = succeed "," do
                %em Operads and motives in deformation quantization
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/9904055"} math/9904055
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1023/A:1007555725247"} doi
          %h3#singlesorted_definition Single-sorted definition
          %p
            It is possible to define torsors using a single-sorted
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+theory"} algebraic theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+spaces"} affine spaces
            can be defined either as sets with a free and transitive action of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
          %p
            More precisely, a
            %strong torsor
            (also known as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heap"} heap
            when stated in a single-sorted form) is a set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            equipped with a ternary operation
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msup
                    %mi T
                    %mn 3
                  %mo →
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t\colon T^3 \to T
          %p such that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo ,
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi b
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo ,
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi d
                  %mo ,
                  %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo ,
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo ,
                  %mi d
                  %mo ,
                  %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t(a,a,b)=t(b,a,a)=b,\qquad t(t(a,b,c),d,e)=t(a,b,t(c,d,e)).
          %p
            A
            %strong homomorphism of torsors
            is a map of sets that preserves this operation.
          %p The equivalence with the two-sorted definition is demonstrated as follows.
          %p
            Given a
            = succeed "-torsor" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            equipped with the ternary operation
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t(a,b,c)=g(a,b)c
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g(a,b)
            is the unique element of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            such that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi b
                    %mo =
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g(a,b)b=a
          %p
            Given a torsor
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo ,
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (T,t)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi LTrans
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (LTrans(T),T)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi LTrans
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} LTrans(T)
            is a subgroup of the group of bijections on the set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            comprising precisely the bijections of the form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo ,
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c\mapsto t(a,b,c)
            for some elements
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a,b\in T
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            acts on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            by evaluation:
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi gt
                    %mo =
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} gt=g(t)
          %p
            Mapping
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mo ,
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↦
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi LTrans
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↦
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mo ,
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (T,t)\mapsto (LTrans(T),T)\mapsto (T,t)
            gives back the same torsor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
